+- **Escalation review (plan T61):** reads the task, the diff and the one recurring P1 it judges, each cut and fenced (the finding as `escalated finding`); it has no tools and no message store, and holds no credential of the project. Its answer is a structured `confirmed` or `rejected` with reasons, validated against its schema; anything else is a failed escalation that keeps no verdict, never a rejection. Plain code acts on the kept verdict: a confirmation sends the next build to the strong tier, a rejection starts one more review round of the change on the same head (at most once per head) and shows the reasons to its reviewers. The reasons are redacted before they are kept, and they reach later reviewers fenced as `escalation verdicts`, so a steered escalation can only move a build to the strong tier, cost one more review round on a head, or give a reviewer an argument it weighs against the code; it closes no finding and passes no change.
